HINA: Aria.
HINA: Why did you let them kill you?
ARIA: Hmm…I wonder.
ARIA: Isn’t it nice that every story has a villainess?
ARIA: If I was meant to die a thousand deaths, then each one should be meaningful.
ARIA: When you allowed me your blood, I accepted my fate.
HINA: …
HINA: Reckless idiot. 
ARIA: And I am yours for eternity.
ARIA: Isn’t that grand?
ARIA: A lifetime of adventure and opulence? 
ARIA: This world is changing. 
ARIA: And we stand on the knife’s edge–! 
HINA: This future you envision.
HINA: Does it have room for us?
ARIA: I don’t particularly care if it does or doesn’t.
ARIA: ~
ARIA: ~~ 
ARIA: What I care about is singing the first song.
HINA: Even at the cost of your song becoming anathema? 
ARIA: This is not a new concept for us, Hinadear.
